      "provenance": "literature_retrieved",
      "rationale": "[Literature audit 2026-11-05 (deliverome-analysis PR 236), verdict confirmed_exact: position confirmed at this residue. validation_level surface_and_function -> surface_only (paper reports surface: yes, function: not_reported). Paper (PMID 31996424): \"kAE1 containing an HA tag within the third extracellular loop between Asn 556 and Val 557 (kAE1 HA )\". Audit note: Human kAE1 (kidney isoform lacking aa 1-65) keeps eAE1 numbering; N556|V557 matches P02730 canonical. Construct expressed in S. cerevisiae: PM localization of kAE1-HA shown by Pma1p colocalization and immunogold EM (not a non-permeabilized stain). pH and chloride (function) assays used untagged kAE1 WT only, so this paper does not support surface_and_function for the HA construct; the other PMCs cited in the rationale were not audited here.] L4 explicitly names the junction as 'between Asn556 and Val557', confirmed by Python: seq[555]='N' (Asn556) and seq[556]='V' (Val557), both within EC3 (542\u2013569). The insert sits 15 residues from the upstream TM boundary (TM5 ends at 541) and 13 residues from the downstream TM boundary (TM6 starts at 570), well beyond the \u22653 residue minimum. No cysteines or NxS/T glycosylation sequons are present in EC3. Independent validation across at least four publications (PMC3584104, PMC6992373, PMC9623938, PMC12959882) with both HA and Myc tags, and explicit functional assays, makes this a high-confidence site. Full-length kAE1 (kidney isoform of SLC4A1) expressed in MDCK cells and yeast with an HA epitope tag inserted between Asn556 and Val557 in the third extracellular loop (EC3, residues 542\u2013569, eAE1 canonical numbering). L4 (PMC6992373) is the most precise pinning: 'HA tag within the third extracellular loop between Asn556 and Val557'. Multiple independent papers (PMC3584104, PMC9623938, PMC12959882) corroborate the same position as 'position 557' in the same loop. A Myc tag at the same position is reported in PMC9623938 (L8).",
      "residue_after": "V",
