  "literature_notes": "Four ledger lines were evaluated. L1 and L2 both pin an HA or Myc tag to eAE1 position 557 in the third extracellular loop (EC3, 542\u2013569); they support the same junction (insert_after_residue=557) and are consolidated into Site 1, with L2 as the primary citation because it provides more experimental detail. L3 pins a V5 tag to the adjacent junction after residue 558 via an explicit flanking-peptide readout; L4 confirms surface display of the same construct and is treated as corroborating evidence for Site 2. Both sites are in EC3, which is the only loop long enough (28 residues) to carry a short epitope tag comfortably; all other extracellular spans in SLC4A1 are 1\u201315 residues (EC1 14 aa, EC2 15 aa, EC4 36 aa, EC5 1 aa, EC6 1 aa, EC7 7 aa). EC4 (625\u2013660, 36 aa) has no ledger-supported insertion and was not proposed. No ledger line supports any terminal tag (the N-terminus is intracellular and the C-terminus is intracellular), so no terminal sites are reported.",
